  "content": "# Travel Journal: The Ascent to Kharang\n\n*Day 14 \u2014 Somewhere above the tree line, Eastern Himalaya*\n\nThe road ended three days ago, where the jeep had groaned and finally refused to climb any further, its wheels spinning uselessly in the mud that seemed to swallow everything we touched. From that point, the real journey began on foot, following a goat path so narrow that the mountain wall pressed against my back on one side and a sheer drop opened up on the other. Dr. Anaya Sharma adjusted the strap of her specimen case, breathing through the thin air that grew sharper with every hundred meters of elevation. She had studied alpine botany for eleven years, but nothing in the textbooks had prepared her for the way the landscape seemed to rewrite itself with each turn of the trail.\n\nThe morning had begun in a fog so dense she could barely see her own boots, each step a careful negotiation with the unknown. But by mid-morning, the weather performed its daily miracle. The gray curtain lifted in fragments, revealing peaks that caught the first light in shades of rose and amber. Anaya paused to record her observations in the leather-bound notebook she'd carried across three continents: temperature 4\u00b0C, humidity dropping rapidly",
